#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-SD1053 expect=skipped domain=TV
#note "The batch's ONLY pin of an INJECTED var_exists guard folding false. TV deliberately carries no ARMCD column. The shipped expression leads with var_exists(\"ARMCD\") (machine-emitted), which is FALSE over an absent column and short-circuits the AND -> zero findings WITH EXECUTION. ARMCD is Exp in TV, so a TV that is not arm-specific legitimately omits it; the rule has no Requirements.Variables gate, so this is a silence, not a skip. PLAN-retire-corpus-transforms phase 4: the rule now declares the gate variable in Requirements.Variables.All, so the absent column takes the auditable SKIP this scenario pins (Fix #330 remedy: a presence rule reports the absence once)."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
dataset TV label="Trial Visits"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col VISITNUM type=Num label="Visit Number"
col VISIT   type=Char label="Visit Name"
---
S1 | TV | 1 | SCREENING
S1 | TV | 2 | WEEK 2
